{"id":"payees-registered-after-first-payment","title":"Payees whose registration opened after a whole year of City payments","question":"Which City payees opened their only San Francisco business registration after the City had already paid them for a whole fiscal year?","finding":"Of 5,770 payees paid $100,000 or more since fiscal 2019, 3,148 match exactly one registry account by name. 21 of those (0.7%) opened that account after a fiscal year in which the City had already paid them, $26.4 million in those years. The largest: Triage LLC, paid $22.1 million by Public Health from fiscal 2021 before an account that opens on 2024-04-22. 2 rows are confirmed by a second address; the rest are name matches.","how":"A payee is joined to the registry when exactly one account carries its name. The account's earliest business start date is compared with the end of each fiscal year of payment (30 June). Payees first paid in fiscal 2019, the first year in the file, are left out, as are payees with an older account under a like name.","limits":"Start dates are reported by the business. An out-of-town firm may owe registration only once it works in the City; a new account can follow a merger or a change of owner while an older account under another name is closed; the registry is a tax record and says nothing about whether work was done. The payee-to-registry join is a name match unless the last column says otherwise.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"payee","t":"City payee","type":"org"},{"k":"paid","t":"Paid since fiscal 2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"dept","t":"Mostly from","type":"text"},{"k":"firstPaid","t":"First paid (fiscal year)","type":"year"},{"k":"registered","t":"Registry account opens","type":"date"},{"k":"paidBefore","t":"Paid in years before it","type":"usd"},{"k":"place","t":"Registered in","type":"text"},{"k":"basis","t":"How joined","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"payee":"Triage LLC","paid":27264504,"dept":"Public Health","firstPaid":2021,"registered":"2024-04-22","paidB